    "created_at": "2017-07-25T15:23:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-07-25T15:23:26Z",
    "body": "The spec for CanvasRenderingContext2D does not need to use the notion of \"CSS pixels\" anywhere. Without HD backings, there is no point in maintaining language that describe a resolution-indepndent coordinate space.  As it currently stands, one unit in CanvasRenderingContext2D space corresponds to the size of a pixel in the canvas's backing store. The us of \"CSS pixels\" is not necessarily incorrect, but it adds unnecessary complexity to the spec IMHO.  \r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
