    "updated_at": "2017-07-25T17:13:59Z",
    "body": "Isn't it incorrect when you can have `<canvas width=200 height=200 style=width:100px;height:100px></canvas>`? That's 100x100 CSS pixels, but 200x200 canvas pixels. And if backed by a 3x display, would be drawn on 300x300x device pixels (creating some artifacts due to the scaling).",
